The cost of equity is the return that a company requires to decide if an investment meets capital return requirements. Firms often use it as a capital budgeting threshold for the required rate of return. The traditional formula for the cost of equity is the dividend capitalization model and the capital asset pricing model (CAPM). is NOT relevant, dump it.
